#!/bin/sh
# The environment of the release. It is picked up by any `bin/sweet <command>`.
#
# brain has NO distribution. By default the release brings up a node and epmd, while the hand
# sits with brain on one network (`sweet_hands`) — access to distribution would mean
# execution of code right in the BEAM, that is, exactly the boundary for the sake of which the hand
# talks to brain in frames over a socket, and not as a node (see Sweet.Hand, BOUNDARY 3).
#
# The price is known and accepted: `bin/sweet remote` and `bin/sweet rpc` do not work.
# The front end is one anyway — IEx through `docker attach` (CMD sets `start_iex`).
export RELEASE_DISTRIBUTION=none
